<h1>Colour Plot Settings</h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>The options in this section concern the colour settings, which will be used in <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> mode.</p>
<p><img src="../INSPECTION_MODE_FILES/colour_plot_settings.gif" width="401px" height="276px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Command">Colour scheme name</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">This listbox contains a list of predefined colour schemes, which can not be overwritten. You can choose one of them or use your own scheme. Rainbow (default) is the default colour scheme.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">You can create your own colour scheme and save it using the <span class="Command">Save as...</span> button.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Command">Delete</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Removes the selected scheme</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Each colour scheme is based on seven main colours - <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Above max</b></span>,<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Main colour1</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Main colour2</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Zero range</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Main colour3</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Main colour4</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Below min</b></span>. Click on a colour and a colour chooser dialog will be shown. There you can choose another colour.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Rainbow</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Represents the colour scale as a gradient</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Discrete</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The gradient is split to a number of colours.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Number of splits</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Defines in how many sections to be split the gradient when using the Discrete mode.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Apply</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets the current scheme to the current page</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Apply to all</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets the current scheme to all inspection pages</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Close</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Closes this dialog</p>
<p class="bullet">&#160;</p>
